      "id": "english-poetry-anthology-s0032-p00066",
      "source_en": "Vigil for comrade swiftly slain, vigil I never forget, how as day brighten'd,\nI rose from the chill ground and folded my soldier well in his blanket,\nAnd buried him where he fell.",
